tinyx - run an X11 session on the framebuffer

SYNOPSIS
    /usr/X11/bin/tinyx
    /usr/X11/bin/tinyx --check
    /usr/X11/bin/tinyx /path/to/client [argument ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Start a Tiny-X server and one client. With no arguments the
    client draws an interactive demo. A click inside the panel or a
    letter key changes its color. Escape ends a graphics session.

    The --check option runs a headless client that paints a window
    and reads it back through the X11 protocol.

    A named client reads X11 replies and events from standard input
    and writes raw requests to standard output. Use standard error
    for text. The server ends when the client exits.

FILES
    /dev/fb0        32 bit screen framebuffer
    /dev/keyboard   translated set 1 keyboard events
    /dev/mouse      relative pointer events
    /dev/touchpad   fallback pointer device
    /usr/X11/COPYING  license for the server

SEE ALSO
    dev(5), tty(5)
